course: dictionary
lesson: 9889
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them are the clues that tell you which meaning is used. «The taipan slid under the rock, and we stepped back at once.» Slid, rock and stepped back are clues about a creature, so taipan means a snake here.
explain: «In the 1800s, the taipan gave orders from his office in Hong Kong.» Gave orders, office and the old date are clues about business, so taipan means a powerful head of a foreign company here. The same word, a different meaning.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: which meaning fits the sentence? Swap your meaning in and check that it still makes sense. A dictionary lists each meaning with a number, so you can test them one by one.
fact: A taipan is a large, very venomous snake from Australia and New Guinea.
fact: The inland taipan has the strongest venom of any land snake, when tested on mice in the laboratory.
fact: The inland taipan is shy and lives in remote areas, so bites are very rare.
fact: If you see a snake, stay still and back away; for a bite, call 000.
fact: In history, a taipan was a powerful head of a foreign business company in Hong Kong and China in the 1800s and early 1900s.
exercise: «The inland taipan lives in remote desert and is very shy.» What kind of animal is the taipan here? | A type of bird | A company boss | *A snake | A kind of fish
exercise: «In the 1800s, the taipan gave orders from his office in Hong Kong.» What does taipan mean here? | A tall tree | A small shop | *A powerful head of a foreign company | A snake from Australia
exercise: If you see a taipan, what should you do? | Throw a stone at it | Run at it | *Stay still and back away | Pick it up to look
test: «Bites from the inland taipan are very rare, because the snake is shy.» Why are bites rare? | The snake only eats fish | The snake is very big and slow | *The snake is shy and lives in remote areas | The snake lives in cities
test: Which sentence uses taipan to mean a business boss? | Stay still when you see a taipan | A taipan slid under the rock | *In 1850 the taipan ran a powerful foreign company in Hong Kong | Call 000 after a snake bite
exam: Which word in «The inland taipan has the strongest venom of any land snake» best shows that taipan is a snake? | the | *venom | inland | strongest
